### Mathematical result (two independent subtasks agreeing)
**Upper bound k ≤ 520.** For sides 1≤w,h≤500 with w+h=s, the minimum area is g(s)=s−1 for s≤501 and g(s)=500(s−500) for s≥502 (concave area minimized at an endpoint). g is nondecreasing: 1,2,…,500, then 1000,1500,…. Distinct s_i force 250000 = Σ area ≥ Σ g(s_i) ≥ sum of the k smallest g-values. The 520 smallest sum to 125250 + 500(2+…+21) = **240250 ≤ 250000**, while the 521 smallest add 500·22 = 11000 → **251250 > 250000**. Hence k ≤ 520.

**Construction with k = 520.** Top strip 500×1 (s=501); left block 250×499 split into 499 unit-width strips with heights 1..499 (s = 2..500); right block 250×499 split into 20 full-height strips of widths 3..22, summing to 250 (s = 502..521). Total 499+1+20 = 520 rectangles, semiperimeters exactly {2,…,521}, area 124750+500+124750 = 250000. I re-verified cell-by-cell on a 500×500 grid: perfect cover, no overlaps, 520 distinct semiperimeters, area 250000.

**Cross-checks.** My exhaustive tiling enumeration gives K(1..8) = 1,1,3,4,6,7,8,9, matching the general formula K_N = N+m with m(m+3) ≤ N−1 (N=500 → m=20 → K=520; n=2 is the lone exception).

